# Build context exclusions for `podman build -f Containerfile` (see `make image`).
#
# This is the single source of truth. Podman and Buildah read .containerignore
# first; Docker and BuildKit only ever look for .dockerignore, so .dockerignore
# is a symlink to this file rather than a second copy that could drift.
# BuildKit follows a symlinked .dockerignore since Docker 18.09.1
# (moby/buildkit#733), so both toolchains apply the exact same rules.
#
# Caveat: a Git checkout on Windows without symlink support (core.symlinks=false)
# materialises .dockerignore as a text file containing ".containerignore", which
# silently drops these exclusions for `docker build`. It never affects podman,
# which reads this file directly, and it costs build-context upload time rather
# than changing the resulting image.

# VCS & tooling
.git
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml
.idea
.vscode
.claude

# Build outputs & caches.
# dist/ is deliberately NOT excluded: the default "prebuilt" build installs
# dist/k8s-kms-plugin, produced by `make build`. Only the non-binary goreleaser
# artifacts are dropped from the context.
build/
*.test
*.out
.socket
dist/*.json
dist/*.txt
dist/*.sig
dist/*.pem
dist/*.tar.gz
dist/*.zip
dist/*.deb
dist/*.rpm
dist/*.apk
dist/*.pkg.tar.zst
dist/artifacts.json
dist/metadata.json
dist/config.yaml

# Dependencies are resolved by `go mod download` inside the builder stage
vendor/

# Local secrets, environment and vendor PKCS#11 clients
.env
*.pem
*.key
files/

# Docs & assets not needed to compile
docs/
*.md

# Deployment manifests, scripts and test fixtures
deployments/
scripts/
test/
